
Comic Craft – Project Design Phase

Since Comic Craft is a small project, the design phase can be kept simple and focused on the main features rather than including complex systems.

1. Purpose of the Design Phase

The Project Design Phase converts the requirements identified earlier into a simple design for how Comic Craft will look and work.

The main goals are to:

Design the basic user interface.

Decide the main screens.

Plan how users create comics.

Decide how comic elements are arranged.

Choose the basic technology and database structure.

Create a simple prototype or wireframe.



---

2. Basic System Design

Comic Craft can have a simple structure:

User → Comic Craft Interface → Comic Editor → Save/Export

The user enters the application, creates a comic using the editor, adds characters and dialogue, and then saves or exports the completed comic.


---

3. Main Screens

For a small Comic Craft project, the system can contain only a few main screens:

Home Page

Comic Craft title/logo

Short introduction

Create Comic button

My Comics button


Comic Creation Page

Comic title

Select template/layout

Start creating the comic


Comic Editor

The main working area where users can:

Add panels

Add characters

Add backgrounds

Add speech bubbles

Add text

Move and resize elements

Save the comic


My Comics

Shows previously saved comics.

Preview/Export

Allows the user to view the finished comic and download it.


---

4. User Interface Design

The interface should be simple and beginner-friendly.

A basic editor layout could be:

Left side:
Characters | Backgrounds | Speech Bubbles

Center:
Comic canvas/panels

Right side:
Editing options

Bottom:
Save | Preview | Export

The design should avoid unnecessary buttons and complicated menus.


---

5. Comic Layout Design

A simple comic could contain 3–6 panels.

Example:

Panel 1	Panel 2

Character + Background	Character + Dialogue
Panel 3	Panel 4


Users can add characters and speech bubbles to each panel.


